IMPORT prelude

-- Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act 2002 (Singapore) -- what a "terrorist act" is (s 2(2) to (5)), the four financing
-- offences (ss 3 to 6) and their penalty (s 6A), the Minister's exemptions (s 7), the duties to disclose (ss 8, 10), tipping-off
-- (s 10B), the reach of the offences outside Singapore (s 34), officers of bodies corporate (s 35), and the fixed penalties in
-- ss 9(4), 14 and 10B.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TSFA2002.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 17 of 2022 (in force 1 July 2022) and First Schedule changes to S 568/2026 (in force 26 August 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties and offences a person,
-- business or practitioner meets. Not encoded: the names in the First Schedule (a list, not a rule), the seizure, restraint and
-- forfeiture procedure of Part 4 beyond the s 14 offence, mutual assistance and extradition (Part 5), the audit-order content
-- (s 9(1), (2)), informer protection (s 10A), s 36 (Public Prosecutor's consent) and s 37 (District Court jurisdiction).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act 2002 -- financing`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2(2) to (5) -- terrorist act`

-- s 2(2): "terrorist act" means the use or threat of action (a) where the action (i) involves serious violence against a person;
-- (ii) serious damage to property; (iii) endangers a person's life; (iv) creates a serious risk to the health or the safety of the
-- public; (v) involves the use of firearms or explosives; (vi) releases dangerous, toxic, radioactive or biological agents; (vii)
-- disrupts any public computer system or communications, banking, utilities, transport or public key infrastructure; (viii) disrupts
-- essential emergency services; or (ix) involves prejudice to public security or national defence; AND (b) where the use or threat
-- is "intended or reasonably regarded as intending to" (i) influence or compel the Government, any other government, or any
-- international organisation, or (ii) intimidate the public -- "and includes any action specified in the Second Schedule".
-- s 2(3): "Despite anything in subsection (2)", a terrorist act does not include activities of military forces of a State in the
-- exercise of their official duties, "to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law".
-- s 2(4): persons, property and the public anywhere, within or outside Singapore.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `involves serious violence against a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves serious damage to property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `endangers a person's life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `creates a serious risk to public health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves firearms or explosives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `releases a dangerous substance, toxic chemical or biological agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disrupts a public computer system or critical service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disrupts essential emergency services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prejudices public security or national defence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is meant to influence or compel a government or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is meant to intimidate the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an offence listed in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is official activity of military forces governed by international law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the harm limb is met` IF
        `the conduct`'s `involves serious violence against a person`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `involves serious damage to property`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `endangers a person's life`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `creates a serious risk to public health or safety`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `involves firearms or explosives`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `releases a dangerous substance, toxic chemical or biological agent`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `disrupts a public computer system or critical service`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `disrupts essential emergency services`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `prejudices public security or national defence`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose limb is met` IF
        `the conduct`'s `is meant to influence or compel a government or international organisation`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is meant to intimidate the public`

-- The s 2(3) carve-out is read as applying to the Second Schedule inclusion too ("Despite anything in subsection (2)").
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a terrorist act` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `is official activity of military forces governed by international law`)
    AND (    (`the harm limb is met` `the conduct` AND `the purpose limb is met` `the conduct`)
         OR  `the conduct`'s `is an offence listed in the Second Schedule`)

§§ `34 -- reach outside Singapore`

-- s 3, 4 and 5 say "Every person"; s 6(1) says "No person in Singapore and no citizen of Singapore outside Singapore"; s 8(1)
-- "Every person in Singapore and every citizen of Singapore outside Singapore"; s 10(1) "Every person in Singapore".
-- s 34(1): EVERY person who, outside Singapore, does what would be an offence under s 3, 4 or 5 "is deemed to commit the act or
-- omission in Singapore". (2): an offence under s 6 or 8 committed by a CITIZEN outside Singapore may be dealt with as if committed
-- within Singapore. Nothing extends s 10 to anyone outside Singapore.
DECLARE Section IS ONE OF
    `section 3`
    `section 4`
    `section 5`
    `section 6`
    `section 8`
    `section 10`

GIVEN `the section` IS A Section, `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section reaches the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 10` THEN `is in Singapore`
    OTHERWISE `is in Singapore` OR `is a Singapore citizen`

§§ `3 and 5 -- financing and using property for a terrorist act`

-- s 3(1): every person who "directly or indirectly, wilfully and without lawful excuse, provides or collects property -- (a) with
-- the intention that the property be used; or (b) knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that the property will be used,
-- in whole or in part, in order to commit any terrorist act".
GIVEN `provides or collects property` IS A BOOLEAN, `acts wilfully and without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `intends or has grounds to believe it is for a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 3` IF
    `provides or collects property` AND `acts wilfully and without lawful excuse` AND `intends or has grounds to believe it is for a terrorist act`

-- s 5(1): every person who (a) "uses property ... for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out any terrorist act"; or (b)
-- "possesses property intending that it be used or knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that it will be used" for that
-- purpose. Use alone is enough under (a); possession needs the intention or belief under (b).
GIVEN `uses property to facilitate or carry out a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN, `possesses property` IS A BOOLEAN, `intends or has grounds to believe it is for a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 5` IF
        `uses property to facilitate or carry out a terrorist act`
    OR  (`possesses property` AND `intends or has grounds to believe it is for a terrorist act`)

§§ `4, 6 and 7 -- supplying terrorists, dealing with their property, and exemptions`

-- s 4(1): every person who "collects property, provides or invites a person to provide, or makes available property or financial or
-- other related services" (a) intending, or knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe, they will be used to facilitate or carry
-- out any terrorist act, or to benefit any person doing so; or (b) "knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that ... they will
-- be used by or will benefit any terrorist or terrorist entity". (No "wilfully and without lawful excuse", unlike s 3.)
-- s 4(3): facilitating a terrorist act includes financing an individual's travel abroad to give or receive terrorist training.
-- s 7(1): the Minister may by order exempt a person "from section 4(1)(b) or 6 or both" -- NOT from s 4(1)(a), 3 or 5.
-- s 7(2): an exemption from s 4(1)(b) "may not be made" for property or services "that will be used by or will benefit a terrorist
-- entity". s 7(3): an exemption may be subject to terms and conditions, including a notice of exemption before it takes effect.
-- That the exemption fails if its conditions are not met is an INFERENCE from s 7(3) and (4).
DECLARE Supply HAS
    `collects, provides, invites or makes available property or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends or has grounds to believe it will facilitate a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has grounds to believe it will be used by or benefit a terrorist or terrorist entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `will benefit a terrorist entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `falls within a Minister's exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the exemption's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply is exempt from section 4(1)(b)` IF
        `the supply`'s `falls within a Minister's exemption order`
    AND `the supply`'s `meets the exemption's conditions`
    AND (NOT `the supply`'s `will benefit a terrorist entity`)

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 4` IF
        `the supply`'s `collects, provides, invites or makes available property or services`
    AND (    `the supply`'s `intends or has grounds to believe it will facilitate a terrorist act`
         OR  (    `the supply`'s `has grounds to believe it will be used by or benefit a terrorist or terrorist entity`
              AND (NOT `the supply is exempt from section 4(1)(b)` `the supply`)))

-- s 6(1): no person in Singapore and no citizen of Singapore outside Singapore may (a) deal in property the person "knows or has
-- reasonable grounds to believe is owned or controlled by or on behalf of any terrorist or terrorist entity"; (b) enter into or
-- facilitate a financial transaction related to such a dealing; or (c) provide financial or related services in respect of it.
-- s 7(2) restricts only exemptions from s 4(1)(b); an exemption from s 6 carries no terrorist-entity bar.
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `the dealer is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dealer is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deals, transacts or provides services in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has grounds to believe the property is a terrorist's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property belongs to a terrorist entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `falls within a Minister's exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the exemption's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6` IF
        `the section reaches the person` `section 6` (`the dealing`'s `the dealer is in Singapore`) (`the dealing`'s `the dealer is a Singapore citizen`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `deals, transacts or provides services in the property`
    AND `the dealing`'s `has grounds to believe the property is a terrorist's`
    AND (NOT (`the dealing`'s `falls within a Minister's exemption order` AND `the dealing`'s `meets the exemption's conditions`))

-- s 7(4): where a person is exempted, "any other person involved in carrying out" the exempted activity "is also exempt from
-- section 4(1)(b) or 6 or both ... and section 8, if the terms and conditions of the exemption (if any) are met".
-- On the words, s 7(1) exempts the NAMED person from s 4(1)(b) and 6 only; only the OTHER persons of s 7(4) are also freed from the
-- s 8 duty to disclose. That reading is literal and may not be what was meant.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the person named in the exemption order`
    `another person involved in the exempted activity`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `the exemption's conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from the section 8 duty to disclose` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `another person involved in the exempted activity` THEN `the exemption's conditions are met`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3(2), 4(2), 5(2), 6(3) -- civil immunity for reasonable measures`

-- ss 3(2), 4(2), 5(2): a person "who acts reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to avoid committing an offence" is not
-- liable in civil proceedings. s 6(3) adds a condition: "if the person took all reasonable steps to satisfy himself, herself or
-- itself that the relevant property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of any terrorist or terrorist entity".
GIVEN `the section` IS A Section, `acted reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps to confirm the property was a terrorist's` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `immune from civil proceedings` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 6` THEN `acted reasonably` AND `took all reasonable steps to confirm the property was a terrorist's`
    WHEN `section 8` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 10` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `acted reasonably`

§§ `6A and 6B -- penalty for the financing offences`

-- s 6A: on conviction under s 3, 4, 5 or 6 -- (a) an individual: fine not exceeding $500,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 10 years
-- or both; (b) in any other case: fine not exceeding "the higher of (i) $1 million; or (ii) twice the value of the property
-- (including funds derived or generated from the property), financial services ..., or financial transaction".
-- s 6B: abetment, conspiracy or attempt -- "the same punishment".
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `value involved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 6A` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN 500000
    ELSE `the higher of` 1000000 (2 TIMES `value involved`)

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years under section 6A` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 10 ELSE 0

§§ `8 -- duty to disclose terrorist property`

-- s 8(1): every person in Singapore and every citizen of Singapore outside Singapore who (a) has possession, custody or control of any
-- property belonging to any terrorist or terrorist entity; or (b) has information about any transaction or proposed transaction in
-- respect of such property "must immediately inform the Commissioner of Police". (2): must give further information if required.
-- (4): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (1) to prove that the person had a reasonable excuse".
-- (6): "Commissioner of Police" includes any police officer.
GIVEN `holds terrorist property or knows of a transaction in it` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed the police immediately` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8(1)` IF
        `holds terrorist property or knows of a transaction in it`
    AND `the section reaches the person` `section 8` `is in Singapore` `is a Singapore citizen`
    AND (NOT `informed the police immediately`)
    AND (NOT `proves a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 8(3): (a) an individual to whom the property or information came "in the course of the person's trade, profession, business or
-- employment" -- $250,000 or 5 years or both; (b) any other individual -- $50,000 or 5 years or both; (c) not an individual -- (i)
-- for contravening (1), the higher of $1 million or twice the value of the property; (ii) for contravening (2), $1 million.
DECLARE Contravention IS ONE OF
    `failing to inform the police`
    `failing to give further information`

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `learnt of it at work` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contravention` IS A Contravention, `value of the property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 8` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `learnt of it at work`
         THEN 250000
         ELSE 50000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the contravention`
         WHEN `failing to inform the police` THEN `the higher of` 1000000 (2 TIMES `value of the property`)
         OTHERWISE 1000000

§§ `10 -- information about terrorism financing`

-- s 10(1): every person IN SINGAPORE who has information which the person knows or believes may be of material assistance in
-- preventing a terrorism financing offence, or in securing the apprehension, prosecution or conviction of another person, "who fails to
-- disclose the information immediately to a police officer shall be guilty of an offence". (3): reasonable excuse is a defence.
GIVEN `has information of material assistance` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed to the police immediately` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10` IF
        `has information of material assistance`
    AND `the section reaches the person` `section 10` `is in Singapore` `is a Singapore citizen`
    AND (NOT `disclosed to the police immediately`)
    AND (NOT `proves a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 10(2): (a) individual, information at work -- $250,000 or 5 years; (b) other individual -- $50,000 or 5 years; (c) not an
-- individual -- (i) "where a terrorism financing offence was committed", the higher of $1 million or twice the value involved; (ii)
-- "where no terrorism financing offence was committed, $1 million".
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `learnt of it at work` IS A BOOLEAN, `a financing offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN, `value involved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 10` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `learnt of it at work`
         THEN 250000
         ELSE 50000
    ELSE IF `a financing offence was committed`
         THEN `the higher of` 1000000 (2 TIMES `value involved`)
         ELSE 1000000

§§ `10B -- tipping-off`

-- s 10B(1): a person who knows or has reasonable grounds to suspect that a police officer is acting or proposing to act in an
-- investigation under this Act and discloses anything "likely to prejudice that investigation"; (2): the same where the person knows or
-- suspects a disclosure or report has been made under s 8, 9 or 10. Fine not exceeding $250,000 or 5 years or both -- "Any person",
-- with no higher fine for a body corporate.
-- (3), (4): no offence for an advocate and solicitor, or legal counsel in an entity, disclosing to the client for advice or for legal
-- proceedings; (7): but not where disclosed "with a view to furthering any illegal purpose". (8): a defence "to prove that the person did
-- not know and had no reasonable ground to suspect that the disclosure was likely to be prejudicial". (9): nothing done in enforcing
-- the Act or other penal legislation.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `knows or suspects an investigation or a report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is likely to prejudice the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is by a lawyer to a client for advice or for legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `furthers an illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proves no reason to suspect prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is done in enforcing the law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the legal-advice exception applies` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `is by a lawyer to a client for advice or for legal proceedings`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `furthers an illegal purpose`)

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tipping-off is an offence` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `knows or suspects an investigation or a report`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `is likely to prejudice the investigation`
    AND (NOT `the legal-advice exception applies` `the disclosure`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `proves no reason to suspect prejudice`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `is done in enforcing the law`)

§§ `9(4), 10B, 14 -- fixed penalties`

-- s 9(4): contravening a Minister's audit order -- $50,000 or 5 years or both. s 10B(1), (2): $250,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 14: contravening a restraint order served under s 11(4) while it is in force -- $50,000 or 5 years or both.
DECLARE OtherOffence IS ONE OF
    `contravening an audit order`
    `tipping-off`
    `contravening a restraint order`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN OtherOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `tipping-off` THEN 250000
    OTHERWISE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN OtherOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `tipping-off` THEN 5
    WHEN `contravening an audit order` THEN 5
    WHEN `contravening a restraint order` THEN 5

§§ `35 -- officers of bodies corporate`

-- s 35: where a company, firm, society or other body commits an offence under this Act, a director, manager, secretary or similar
-- officer or partner "shall be guilty of that offence ... unless he or she proves that -- (a) the offence was committed without his or
-- her consent or connivance; AND (b) he or she had exercised all such due diligence to prevent the commission of the offence".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an officer or partner` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence`
    AND `is an officer or partner`
    AND (NOT (`proves no consent or connivance` AND `proves due diligence`))
